# liblouis: Unified English Braille Code New Zealand Māori (Grade 1)
#
#-name: New Zealand Māori
#-index-name: Māori, New Zealand
#-display-name: Māori braille as used in New Zealand
#+language:mi
#+type:literary
#+contraction:no
#+grade:1
#+system:ubc-nz
#
# This table implements the policy of the Braille Authority of New Zealand Aotearoa Trust relating to translating words in the Māori language into braille, (see https://www.banzat.org.nz/documents/BANZATPolicy8TranscribingMaoriTextInBraille.docx ). This table is for converting Māori text into grade 1 braille, noting that Māori is the indigenous language of New Zealand and currently has no grade 2 braille code.
#
#  This file is part of liblouis.
#
#  liblouis is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it
#  under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public License as
